  "modified": "2026-09-17T17:58:27Z",
  "details": "- CVE-2026-19385: stop pg_dump's dumpFunc() from parsing pg_proc.protrftypes\n  into a fixed FUNC_MAX_ARGS-sized array. parseOidArray() now allocates the\n  array itself and, in the new arraysize < 0 mode used by dumpFunc(), always\n  leaves a zero terminator, so the \"for (i = 0; typeids[i]; i++)\" loop can no\n  longer read past the end of the allocation when the server sends exactly\n  FUNC_MAX_ARGS or more transform type OIDs (heap buffer overflow, CVSS 8.8;\n  upstream REL_14_STABLE 57aa21f, shipped in 14.24)",
